From: OpenATV <info@openatv.org>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: preserve the librtlsdr.so.0 ABI name

OpenATV applications already link to the established librtlsdr.so.0
SONAME.  The old-dab fork does not assign a SONAME to its shared target,
which would leave only an unversioned development-library filename.
Keep the existing runtime ABI and package layout when switching drivers.

diff --git a/src/CMakeLists.txt b/src/CMakeLists.txt
index 0ae6a27..65fab1e 100644
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -38,5 +38,7 @@ endif()
 set_target_properties(rtlsdr_shared PROPERTIES DEFINE_SYMBOL "rtlsdr_EXPORTS")
 set_target_properties(rtlsdr_shared PROPERTIES OUTPUT_NAME rtlsdr)
+set_target_properties(rtlsdr_shared PROPERTIES SOVERSION 0)
+set_target_properties(rtlsdr_shared PROPERTIES VERSION 0.0.0)
 
 ########################################################################
 # Setup static library variant
-- 
2.43.0
